<%# Same shape as the other trigger infos (_indicator_limit_info, _price_drop_limit_info): a
    `small-info` block under the sentence — that class is what makes it a full-width line rather
    than flowing into the sentence — rendered only while the rule is active, going green when the
    trigger's criteria are currently met.

    The drift readout is also the only place a below-minimum rebalance is visible: those are
    deliberately silent, since they repeat every poll for as long as the drift lasts. %>
<% if bot.id.present? && bot.rebalance_enabled? %>
  <small id="<%= bot.new_record? ? "new-settings-rebalance-info" : "settings-rebalance-info" %>" class="small-info">
    <%# The standing explanation first, then the live readout under it: the note describes what the
        rule IS, the readout is what it happens to say right now. %>
    <div><%= t("bot.settings.rebalance.note") %></div>
    <%# A halted swap reads no drift, and its Resume is in the metrics panel (composition/_metrics): a halt
        blocks every tick until resolved, so it has to be reachable whether this rule is on or not,
        and while a selling basket hides the rule altogether. %>
    <% unless bot.rebalance_ambiguous? %>
      <% drift = bot.rebalance_drift %>
      <% if drift.present? %>
        <% tripped = drift > bot.rebalance_threshold %>
        <%# Green means "this will act". A band that is breached but cannot produce a trade above the
            venue minimum must not read as criteria met — on a many-asset index that state can last
            indefinitely, and painting it green is how it goes unnoticed. %>
        <% blocked = tripped && bot.rebalance_below_minimum? %>
        <div class="<%= "text-success" if tripped && !blocked %>">
          <%= t("bot.settings.rebalance.drift", drift: (drift * 100).round(1)) %>
          <%= t("bot.settings.rebalance.below_minimum") if blocked %>
        </div>
      <% end %>
    <% end %>
  </small>
<% end %>
